  - '.github/workflows/feature-matrix.yml'
  # [OPUS-4.8] sq-ibrze: editing a per-crate fragment (adding/changing an
  # opt-in leg) or the assembler MUST re-run the full matrix so the new/edited
  # leg actually builds+tests — even on an otherwise non-Rust PR.
  - '.github/feature-matrix.d/**'
  - 'scripts/assemble-feature-matrix.py'
  # [FABLE-5] PR #3511 review finding 2: the grouped-runner engine is as
  # load-bearing as the assembler — a PR changing ONLY this script must
  # still run setup (its self-test gates there) + the grouped execution
  # + the reporter. Wiring pinned by test_feature_matrix_assemble.py.
  - 'scripts/run-feature-matrix-group.py'
  # [FABLE-5] PR #3511 review round-3 finding 2: the PRIVILEGED reporter
  # workflow is the trust-boundary half of finding 1. A PR changing ONLY
  # .github/workflows/feature-matrix-report.yml would otherwise skip setup,
  # so its dedicated trusted-boundary self-tests (run in setup) never run —
  # a change to the privileged reporter must re-run them. Wiring pinned by
  # test_feature_matrix_assemble.py.
  - '.github/workflows/feature-matrix-report.yml'
  # [FABLE-5] PR #3511 review finding 4: the assembler/runner self-test is
  # the mechanized guard for the gate-critical leg-name contract AND the
  # trusted-boundary wiring. A test-only edit that WEAKENS it must still
  # re-run the setup self-test (which runs this file) — otherwise a PR
  # could gut the guard while skipping the very job that enforces it.
  - 'scripts/tests/test_feature_matrix_assemble.py'

